    "scriptCode": "// --- BORROMEAN RINGS ---\n// Three ellipses in the three coordinate planes, semi-axes 1 and 2: no two of\n// them are linked, yet the three cannot be pulled apart. One tube per\n// MESH_BEGIN section; `mesh` (0, 1, 2) picks the plane by cycling the\n// coordinates of the same ellipse. In each section the v line only sets the\n// steps around the tube: 32 for every 200 along the curve.\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\nvec3 q = vec3(cos(u), 2.0*sin(u), 0.0);\nvec3 r = (mesh < 0.5) ? q : ((mesh < 1.5) ? q.zxy : q.yzx);\nreturn vec4(r / 1.5, 0.0);\n",
